# rule.forbid.shouts

acronyms stay lowercase — no all-caps shouts: `jwt`, `api`, `cli`, `json`, `readme.md`, `src/api/`
scope: names (vars, functions, types), comments, filenames, dirs, docs, logs, commits, pr text
why: all-caps demands undue attention, adds no info for a known term, and collides in camelcase
camelcase: treat an acronym as a plain word — `getJwtToken`, `parseJson`
enforcement: an all-caps acronym = blocker
see also: rule.prefer.lowercase · rule.require.ubiqlang
